From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] hdcp/samsung: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx)

Port private/google-modules/hdcp/samsung to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - platform_driver.remove returns void (6.11)

Files: main.c

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

lynx-linus-mainline (android-mainline -> Linus' v7.3; ACK-only interfaces are
handled here rather than restored in the kernel, see kernel/patches/README.md):
  * Kbuild for the ddk_modules here, generated from BUILD.bazel by
    tools/bazel2kbuild.py, for the make-only build (kernel/kbuild.mk):
      Kbuild
---
diff --git a/Kbuild b/Kbuild
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b46f2bd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Kbuild
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
